'' A QUALIFIED TYPE NAME IS ARITY-CHECKED AS A PLAIN ONE IS (T87). T82 judged a constructor
'' call only when its target was a bare name, so 'Geo.P( 1, 2 )' -- and the book's own
'' 'chrono.TimeSpan( 0, 1, 30, 0 )' -- compiled with no diagnostic and built an undefined
'' value; the chrono call crashed. See src/symbols/ctorargs.bas, CheckCtorCallArgs_.
''
'' MEASURED, fbc-modern 1.20 with -maxerr inf over the source, 2026-10-03: error 1 on lines
'' 23, 24 and 26, error 99 on 25, and no others: a namespace, a typed 'dim', an overload set
'' and a nested namespace with a defaulted parameter. Lines 27-29 are the arities fbc
'' accepts. (A one-argument call with a value of the type itself stays unjudged, qualified or
'' not -- see ctor-arg-accepted.test.)
